# 3. Recommended Technical Architecture

Use current stable technologies.

Preferred architecture:

## Monorepo

Use a monorepo so web, mobile and shared domain logic remain synchronized.

Suggested structure:

```text
/apps
  /web
  /mobile

/packages
  /domain
  /formula-engine
  /safety-engine
  /database
  /api
  /validation
  /design-tokens
  /shared-types
  /ai-context
```

### Desktop / Web

Use:

- TypeScript
- React
- Next.js
- Responsive PWA architecture

The web application should be optimized primarily as the professional desktop formulation workspace while remaining responsive.

Optionally make it packageable later using Tauri if a native desktop application becomes useful.

### Mobile

Use:

- React Native
- Expo
- TypeScript

The mobile app should focus especially on:

- sensory evaluation
- voice notes
- quick formula lookup
- raw material lookup
- inventory lookup
- experiment logging
- scent-memory logging
- notifications

### Backend

Prefer:

- PostgreSQL
- Supabase or equivalent PostgreSQL-based backend
- Google OAuth
- secure object storage
- realtime synchronization
- Row Level Security
- server-side validation

Formula-related data is highly relational, so prefer a relational database rather than a document-only database.

